WEBVTT

00:00:01.252 --> 00:00:05.464
Please keep what I'm about to sing

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:08.926
<i>Just between us, okay?</i>

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:14.724
<i>The truth is, I want to keep my
desires hidden deep in my heart</i>

00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:16.851
<i>A secret, a secret</i>

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.703
<i>I</i> want <i>to take shortcuts</i>

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:39.582
<i>Never getting soaked by the rain</i>

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:43.211
<i>Never getting knocked over by the wind</i>

00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:47.006
<i>Even if that's being devious, smile</i>

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:51.469
<i>Even if I'm a coward, play with me</i>

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.056
<i>I don't</i> want <i>to feel sad</i>

00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:58.935
<i>Never getting soaked by tears</i>

00:00:59.018 --> 00:01:02.563
<i>Never feeling at my wit's end</i>

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:06.025
<i>Just smile and think I'm insensitive</i>

00:01:06.108 --> 00:01:11.072
<i>Only tell me about fun things</i>

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:19.372
<i>See, there are faces I</i> want <i>to
see and voices I</i> want <i>to hear</i>

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:24.252
<i>When I wake up I trumpet my joy:</i>

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:30.299
Good morning!
Let's have another fine day!

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:30.967
"Princess Jellyfish"

00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:36.973
<i>Dear Mother,</i>

00:01:37.056 --> 00:01:39.892
I've been having fun lately.

00:01:39.976 --> 00:01:42.812
<i>I found a neat place in the neighborhood.</i>

00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:45.690
<i>It's a no-boys-allowed domain of maidens.</i>

00:01:45.773 --> 00:01:49.777
<i>Actually, I guess it's more like</i> a <i>"den of geeks</i> "...?

00:01:57.368 --> 00:02:01.956
Shu, your uncle will be
here soon. Where's Kuranosuke?

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:03.833
<i>I'll</i> go call him down.

00:02:05.084 --> 00:02:07.044
Are you ready yet, Kuranosuke?

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:09.922
I'm coming in!

00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:16.178
Hello there, dear brother!

00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:19.432
"Enchanted"

00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:25.604
Kuranosuke, do you understand
who's coming to this luncheon?

00:02:25.688 --> 00:02:29.734
Of course I do! Uncle Saburota, right?

00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:31.527
You intend to meet him dressed like that?!

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:37.408
Why not? After all, I used some extra
padding as a service to the old guys!

00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:43.581
Shu! Kuranosuke! Your uncle is here!

00:02:43.664 --> 00:02:45.041
Okay!

00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:54.467
You... You... What's with you?
What's going on in your head?

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.345
It's just bizarre to
suddenly start cross-dressing

00:02:57.428 --> 00:02:59.597
the minute you get to college!

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:09.607
Hiya! It's Masaharu Fukuyama!

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.317
Oh no, he's already here!

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.486
His jokes are as lame as ever.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:16.322
--Go change clothes! --Nah, it's fine!
Anyway, thanks to my cross-dressing,

00:03:16.405 --> 00:03:19.367
I've made friends from a whole new genre.

00:03:20.201 --> 00:03:25.164
I believe in the underlying
strength of all my countrymen!

00:03:25.164 --> 00:03:25.289
"Japan's Underlying Strength"

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.918
You see more and more of
these commercials lately.

00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:30.878
I wonder if there's an election coming up?

00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:34.965
What I want to know is, what nation
would have a balding prime minister?!

00:03:35.049 --> 00:03:38.761
Tap the underlying strength
of your hair follicles first, I say!

00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:41.806
H-He's related to
someone in the area, isn't he?

00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:44.392
Yes, I told you, it's Koibuchi!

00:03:44.392 --> 00:03:45.726
"Koibuchi"

00:03:45.726 --> 00:03:47.645
Prime Minister Negishi is
Koibuchi's wife's brother.

00:03:47.728 --> 00:03:49.772
You saw them on TV before, remember?

00:03:49.855 --> 00:03:54.860
After all, they've been a family
of politicians since before the War.

00:03:54.944 --> 00:03:59.281
Tsukimi, what's the matter?!
There's ectoplasm coming out of your mouth!

00:03:59.365 --> 00:04:02.326
Thank you for taking time
from your busy schedule for us.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:09.166
<i>--Un<:le!</i> I <i>saw</i> your <i>commercial! --Why am I
always dressed like this lately, you ask?</i>

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.293
<i>For two reasons:</i>

00:04:11.377 --> 00:04:16.006
<i>First of all, because a politician
is the last thing I ever want to be!</i>

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.260
<i>So it'll be easier on me later if
people think I'm some kind of deviant!</i>

00:04:19.343 --> 00:04:21.971
<i>--Leave everything to Shu-Shu! --I want to
leave the family birthright to this guy</i>

00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:24.223
<i>and live a life of freedom!</i>

00:04:24.306 --> 00:04:26.809
KUFa-pygn!

00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:29.311
What a cutie-pie you are!

00:04:29.395 --> 00:04:32.523
Hey, Kuranosuke's
pretty good-looking, isn't he?

00:04:32.606 --> 00:04:36.277
Y-Yeah... though he's a bona fide man...

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.197
--Oh, my Kura-pyon! Kura-pyon!
--Kuranosuke! Give it a rest!

00:04:40.281 --> 00:04:43.117
Aw, what's the big deal? It's cute, isn't it?

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.536
I dolled myself up for Uncle!

00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:47.538
D-Dear...

00:04:47.621 --> 00:04:49.832
Such a cutie-pie!

00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:52.877
Get out of my sight this minute!

00:04:54.628 --> 00:04:56.297
Thank goodness!

00:04:56.380 --> 00:05:01.552
Like hell do I want to do lunch with
some old fogeys on such a nice day.

00:05:06.515 --> 00:05:09.101
You look especially fashionable today.

00:05:09.185 --> 00:05:10.561
Thanks!

00:05:11.187 --> 00:05:13.689
Man, I'm impressed Shu can stand to eat

00:05:13.772 --> 00:05:17.359
while they're giving those
boring lectures about politics.

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:23.324
Hello!

00:05:23.407 --> 00:05:25.659
Kuranosuke, when are you coming tonight?

00:05:25.743 --> 00:05:27.661
Oh, what's tonight again?

00:05:27.745 --> 00:05:30.998
I told you, Koji's doing an event in Shimokita!

00:05:31.081 --> 00:05:32.374
Oh, right...

00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:34.251
You're coming, aren't you?

00:05:35.252 --> 00:05:37.338
I'll pass.

00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:38.589
Why?! You up to something else?

00:05:38.672 --> 00:05:43.010
<i>--These days it's just no fun
hanging out with them. "Sorry.</i>

00:05:43.093 --> 00:05:46.889
<i>They only ever talk about
music and fashion and sex.</i>

00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:56.232
The clouds look like jellyfish...

00:05:56.315 --> 00:06:03.280
<i>Yeah, her jellyfish talk is a hundred
times more interesting than that stuff.</i>

00:06:09.411 --> 00:06:12.122
Wow, I didn't know you had
to take them out of the tank

00:06:12.206 --> 00:06:14.625
every time you fed them.

00:06:14.708 --> 00:06:17.002
Say, what <i>do</i> you feed them?

00:06:17.086 --> 00:06:20.673
J-Just normal cultured zooplankton.

00:06:22.967 --> 00:06:27.555
E-Er, may I ask you something?

00:06:27.638 --> 00:06:32.601
Today's theme? You could say it's
"French Lolita crossed with Flapper."

00:06:32.685 --> 00:06:35.062
No, I mean, it's about the fa-fa-fa--

00:06:35.145 --> 00:06:35.980
Fafigirl?

00:06:36.063 --> 00:06:38.357
No, not "fangirl"...

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:43.779
I-I've been told that your honored
f-family does I-important work...

00:06:43.862 --> 00:06:44.989
Work?

00:06:45.072 --> 00:06:47.074
Oh, Meat.

00:06:47.157 --> 00:06:50.869
Hey, you! Would you mind
not calling people "Meat"?

00:06:50.953 --> 00:06:53.372
Where's the meat today?
Where's the Matsusaka beef?

00:06:53.455 --> 00:06:55.207
Isn't there any, Meat?

00:06:55.291 --> 00:06:58.460
B-Banba! We have anmitsu today!

00:06:58.544 --> 00:07:00.170
Anmitsu?! From what shop?!

00:07:00.254 --> 00:07:01.755
This way! This way!

00:07:01.839 --> 00:07:04.174
Chieko! Chieko!

00:07:04.258 --> 00:07:09.471
Yes, yes, it's the anmitsu from
Kinozen that you love so much!

00:07:09.597 --> 00:07:14.768
--Mayaya bought it for us on her way home from a Three
Kingdoms dojinshi event! --3,8OO yen? That's expensive!

00:07:14.852 --> 00:07:16.895
Wow, there's even green tea Bavarian cream!

00:07:16.979 --> 00:07:19.607
--Hey, can I ask a question?
--Anmitsu! Anmitsu!

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:24.069
“Calm down, Banba...
"What do you all do for a living?

00:07:27.323 --> 00:07:31.994
I mean, jellyfish food and
tanks are seriously expensive,

00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:34.997
and the anmitsu at Kinozen is 680 yen!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:40.002
I thought maybe you were students,
but you never seem to go to school...

00:07:40.085 --> 00:07:41.170
Clara here!

00:07:41.253 --> 00:07:46.342
Coming in at #1 on this week's "Top Five
Things You Shouldn't Ask the Sisterhood":

00:07:46.342 --> 00:07:49.762
"What do you do for a living?"

00:07:49.845 --> 00:07:52.389
How old are you, anyway?

00:07:52.473 --> 00:07:54.516
Are those your only questions, Wench?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.769
Well then, let me answer the first:

00:07:56.852 --> 00:07:59.688
we of the Sisterhood have a
respectable source of income!

00:07:59.772 --> 00:08:00.564
It's...

00:08:00.606 --> 00:08:01.774
Yes?

00:08:07.613 --> 00:08:09.573
...our allowances!

00:08:13.452 --> 00:08:17.331
L-Is that really something you
should put on your game face to say...?

00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:21.585
Our parents are the baby boomer generation,

00:08:21.669 --> 00:08:26.048
said to boast the greatest
wealth in all of Japan's long history.

00:08:26.048 --> 00:08:27.257
"Arrival of the Bubble Economy"

00:08:27.633 --> 00:08:31.345
"The Frenzied Masses"

00:08:31.345 --> 00:08:36.850
were forced to live our youth in the
"lost decade" after the bubble burst,

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:39.561
"Ice Age of Hiring"

00:08:39.561 --> 00:08:39.978
"Ice Age of Hiring" "Self-Support" and making it
impossible for us to earn enough to support ourselves on!

00:08:39.978 --> 00:08:43.273
"Ice Age of Hiring" "Self-Support" "impossible" and making
it impossible for us to earn enough to support ourselves on!

00:08:43.357 --> 00:08:45.526
Therefore, there is no shame

00:08:45.609 --> 00:08:47.945
in receiving economic support
from the previous generation--!

00:08:48.028 --> 00:08:53.534
You can stop, Mayaya!
We know! We all understand!

00:08:53.617 --> 00:08:58.497
Wait, boomer children? So that
means you're all in your thirties?!

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.500
Y-You would ask a
woman her age?! How rude!

00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:03.377
I'm eight.

00:09:04.253 --> 00:09:06.922
Banba was born in a leap year.

00:09:07.005 --> 00:09:10.634
Yep. February 29th. So I'm still eight.

00:09:10.718 --> 00:09:13.345
So, to summarize...

00:09:13.429 --> 00:09:17.975
This is like a lair of jobless
thirtysomething NEET chicks with afros?

00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:22.312
What kind of summary is that?!
And no one said we were jobless!

00:09:22.396 --> 00:09:26.233
I work from home stuffing
direct mail envelopes.

00:09:26.316 --> 00:09:31.697
Chieko runs an all-made-to-order online shop.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:37.077
We're also assistants to Ms. Juon Mejiro,
the popular BL manga creator.

00:09:37.161 --> 00:09:40.539
Furthermore! As Chieko is
the daughter of our landlady,

00:09:40.622 --> 00:09:43.959
she is charged with this
building's care in place of her mother,

00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:46.920
who flies to Korea at a
moment's notice in pursuit of Bae!

00:09:47.004 --> 00:09:48.839
--Bae as in that Bae?
--That's the one!

00:09:48.922 --> 00:09:49.923
These are natural curls.

00:09:50.007 --> 00:09:53.469
Therefore! We are! Most definitely! Not!

00:09:53.552 --> 00:09:55.345
NEETs!

00:09:58.056 --> 00:10:02.102
It's so weird how pissed off they got...

00:10:02.186 --> 00:10:04.313
Did I really say something that bad?

00:10:04.396 --> 00:10:05.606
Yes.

00:10:05.689 --> 00:10:08.317
Really?

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.154
Oh, hey, you were asking me
something before. What was it?

00:10:12.237 --> 00:10:18.202
Um... I saw your f-father
and your brother on TV.

00:10:19.995 --> 00:10:23.373
Yeah, they're on all the time these days, huh?

00:10:23.457 --> 00:10:25.292
Wearing really lame ties, too.

00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:31.340
Wh-Why is the son of a
politician dressing like that?

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.760
You want to know?

00:10:41.767 --> 00:10:44.978
Tsukimi, when I really look at you...

00:10:45.062 --> 00:10:46.855
Wanna come to my place?

00:10:46.939 --> 00:10:49.483
It'll be our little secret.

00:10:49.566 --> 00:10:51.235
Let's have some fun.

00:11:01.578 --> 00:11:02.621
It's commercial time!

00:11:02.704 --> 00:11:04.081
Clara!

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.124
It's the second half!

00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:07.042
Tequila!

00:11:16.385 --> 00:11:21.682
First things first: take off... those... rags!

00:11:21.765 --> 00:11:25.143
Let your hair down!

00:11:25.227 --> 00:11:26.645
Pluck your eyebrows!

00:11:26.728 --> 00:11:28.146
Shave!

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:32.192
<i>And the second reason I dress the way I do:</i>

00:11:33.777 --> 00:11:37.698
<i>I want to live in the fashion
world, not the political world!</i>

00:11:37.781 --> 00:11:41.159
Finishing Makeup!

00:11:46.832 --> 00:11:49.585
Kuranosuke, are you home?

00:11:49.668 --> 00:11:52.629
Uncle's on his way out.
Change your clothes and go--

00:12:02.931 --> 00:12:04.516
Hey!

00:12:06.602 --> 00:12:09.187
Hold it right there!

00:12:11.815 --> 00:12:14.776
S-Sorry I slammed it open so hard...

00:12:17.654 --> 00:12:19.197
That's that, then.

00:12:19.281 --> 00:12:21.450
Roger Dodger.

00:12:21.533 --> 00:12:24.912
It's another cutie-pie!

00:12:25.704 --> 00:12:31.001
<i>No... No! I don't</i> want <i>to look like this!</i>

00:12:31.084 --> 00:12:35.923
<i>h' the Sisterhood sees me
like this, they'll brand me a traitor</i>

00:12:36.006 --> 00:12:40.385
<i>and stage my ritual humiliation
on the Otome Road in ikebukuro!</i>

00:12:47.726 --> 00:12:48.852
Yeah.

00:12:48.936 --> 00:12:51.480
Kuranosuke, could you come over right now?

00:12:51.563 --> 00:12:53.815
My outfit and my makeup
just aren't working at all!

00:12:53.899 --> 00:12:56.151
Nah, I'll pass for today.

00:12:56.234 --> 00:12:57.444
What?!

00:12:57.527 --> 00:13:00.864
You guys might not be enough for me anymore.

00:13:00.948 --> 00:13:01.907
Huh?

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.618
See, I've discovered that
polishing the diamond in the rough

00:13:04.701 --> 00:13:06.620
is a hundred times more fun!

00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:11.333
--What's that supposed to mean?! --And so, Mom,
the time has come to put my skills to the test!

00:13:11.416 --> 00:13:14.628
<i>I'm sure even the freaky spinsters of Otaku Land</i>

00:13:14.711 --> 00:13:17.965
<i>want to be pretty too, deep down.</i>

00:13:18.048 --> 00:13:21.843
<i>After all, they were all born princesses.</i>

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:28.642
<i>I was wrong, Mom. He's not a princess at all.</i>

00:13:28.642 --> 00:13:35.983
"Fake Boobs"

00:13:35.983 --> 00:13:36.149
<i>Why would he do this to me of all people?</i>

00:13:36.233 --> 00:13:40.612
<i>To be frank, I can only assume
it's some new form of bullying.</i>

00:13:41.947 --> 00:13:44.449
"No Boys Allowed "

00:13:44.449 --> 00:13:45.200
Good, there's nobody around...

00:13:55.836 --> 00:13:56.503
"Shockingdomll"

00:13:57.004 --> 00:14:00.007
What happened, Banba?! Who did this to you?!

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:04.261
Among men, LL] Bu; among horses, Red Hare!

00:14:06.471 --> 00:14:07.222
“Chieko! Chieko!

00:14:07.222 --> 00:14:09.141
--Mayaya, that hurts.
"Chieko! Chieko!

00:14:09.224 --> 00:14:11.977
A Kijimuna has invaded our Nunnery!

00:14:11.977 --> 00:14:12.019
"Wrong Wei"

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:13.270
Clara!

00:14:13.353 --> 00:14:15.772
What's all this fuss about?

00:14:15.856 --> 00:14:20.819
Tsukimi! What happened to your face?!
You look like a Chinese hopping vampire!

00:14:22.696 --> 00:14:24.656
Heh, she totally does.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:28.326
Then those clothes must
be part of your cosplay!

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.247
She stood up!

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:35.667
--Your fangs shall never pierce my
carotid artery! --Mayaya, that hurts.

00:14:35.751 --> 00:14:37.169
I won't let you get away!

00:14:37.252 --> 00:14:41.089
Wards! Get some wards!

00:14:41.173 --> 00:14:44.760
Mayaya, you're stepping on Banba's hair.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.599
Th-That was close...

00:14:51.016 --> 00:14:56.354
Glasses... I know I have an old cracked pair...

00:14:56.438 --> 00:15:00.233
Here we go, the ones I bought in high school.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:06.406
A... A ghoul?

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:11.453
Sheesh, Tsukimi left her
glasses and her clothes here.

00:15:14.206 --> 00:15:17.751
Kuranosuke, th-there's
something I want to ask you...

00:15:17.834 --> 00:15:21.630
Um... About before... H-How...

00:15:21.713 --> 00:15:25.092
How do you feel about the sales tax increase?!

00:15:25.175 --> 00:15:25.967
I'm against it.

00:15:26.009 --> 00:15:27.385
I see.

00:15:31.181 --> 00:15:32.182
Kuranosuke.

00:15:32.265 --> 00:15:34.059
What do you want?!

00:15:34.142 --> 00:15:37.854
About before... How do you
know that girl? I mean, woman?

00:15:37.938 --> 00:15:41.108
Is she a friend from school or something?

00:15:42.442 --> 00:15:44.402
You've got a crush?!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.782
Well, fancy that! So she's your type, then?

00:15:48.865 --> 00:15:51.118
N-No! What are you talking about?

00:15:51.201 --> 00:15:52.577
Want me to introduce you?

00:15:53.537 --> 00:15:57.874
In exchange, tell me Mom's address.

00:15:57.958 --> 00:16:00.127
You know it, don't you, Bro?

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:04.631
Tell me. I want to see her.

00:16:04.714 --> 00:16:08.593
That again? I've told you before: I don't know.

00:16:08.677 --> 00:16:10.345
By the way...

00:16:10.428 --> 00:16:11.805
...she's a virgin!

00:16:13.223 --> 00:16:15.684
She's a really great girl, you know.

00:16:15.767 --> 00:16:18.186
These days you rarely meet
people so earnest, so sweetly innocent.

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.855
<i>Or to put it another way, "socially reluctant."</i>

00:16:19.938 --> 00:16:21.356
Her hobby is art.

00:16:21.439 --> 00:16:23.358
<i>She only draws jellyfish.</i>

00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:25.360
She's a fine lady.

00:16:25.443 --> 00:16:27.237
<i>Though she's also a NEET nun.</i>

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:30.907
I really think she'd be the
perfect politician's bride.

00:16:33.118 --> 00:16:34.494
Bride...

00:16:34.578 --> 00:16:36.538
She lives right nearby!

00:16:36.621 --> 00:16:40.417
You know, in that retro building
that looks like it's from the late '20s.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.879
Do you mean Amamizu-kan, on Block 3?

00:16:43.962 --> 00:16:47.090
Hey, I'm impressed you know
the name. Leave it to a Diet secretary!

00:16:47.174 --> 00:16:49.593
No, it's because the redevelopment proj--

00:16:49.676 --> 00:16:52.804
Here, she forgot these.
Her glasses and clothes.

00:16:52.888 --> 00:16:55.056
Bro, you go deliver them for her right now!

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.641
<i>While she's still wearing makeup!</i>

00:16:56.725 --> 00:17:02.898
Her name is Tsukimi,
written like "moon" and "sea."

00:17:04.316 --> 00:17:06.526
"Tsukimi"...

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:09.154
"Tsukimi," eh?

00:17:09.237 --> 00:17:10.822
We're here.

00:17:16.995 --> 00:17:19.289
"Shu-Shu's Delusion Time Begins!"

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:27.422
Why, if it isn't Kuranosuke's older brother!

00:17:27.505 --> 00:17:29.674
You forgot these.

00:17:29.758 --> 00:17:33.178
You came all this way to deliver them?

00:17:33.261 --> 00:17:36.848
Please, come inside. I'll make some tea!

00:17:42.812 --> 00:17:48.318
I've always wanted a chance to talk with you.

00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:49.986
Tsukimi...

00:18:08.004 --> 00:18:10.173
Evil spirit, begone!

00:18:12.133 --> 00:18:17.722
<i>H-His brother?! Wait, I think I just ran by</i> him...

00:18:18.181 --> 00:18:20.141
<i>Why is he here?</i>

00:18:22.227 --> 00:18:24.271
You came all this way to deliver them?

00:18:24.354 --> 00:18:27.107
Th-Thank you very much.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:32.112
Um... those are for a lady
named Tsukimi, who lives here...

00:18:32.195 --> 00:18:35.657
Yes, that's right. Thank you.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:39.452
Girls! I made some nice dokudami tea!

00:18:39.536 --> 00:18:43.498
--Snack time! Snack time! --Oh, yay! Dokudami!
Dokudami! That'll drive the chills out!

00:18:43.581 --> 00:18:50.213
Today we have the snack that
Rakuten ranks #1: the green tea roll!

00:18:50.297 --> 00:18:53.341
Rolling! Rolling! Green tea rolling!

00:18:53.425 --> 00:18:58.430
Snack time! Snack time! Snack time!

00:18:58.513 --> 00:19:03.685
Dokudami featuring a green tea rolling!

00:19:04.311 --> 00:19:05.729
What is this place?

00:19:05.812 --> 00:19:09.566
Say, didn't I see a suspicious
man in a suit outside?

00:19:09.649 --> 00:19:12.235
Must've been a salesman or a canvasser.

00:19:31.504 --> 00:19:33.923
Ugh.

00:19:34.007 --> 00:19:37.594
<i>We should tear that place
down for redevelopment ASAP.</i>

00:19:39.054 --> 00:19:42.349
If the younger brother
is a flashy flower hat jelly,

00:19:42.432 --> 00:19:44.809
the intellectual older brother

00:19:44.893 --> 00:19:49.147
is the "cool" character of the
jellyfish world: Sanderia malayensis!

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:52.192
Th-They could be twins!

00:19:53.651 --> 00:19:59.157
Huh, but the human brothers don't
look anything alike, do they Clara?

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:01.284
Welcome home! How'd it go?

00:20:01.368 --> 00:20:03.078
Did you get to see Tsukimi?

00:20:03.161 --> 00:20:06.664
The only ones there were
a bunch of creepy wackjobs.

00:20:06.748 --> 00:20:10.168
Was one of them a braided girl with glasses?

00:20:10.251 --> 00:20:12.879
Yes, she was particularly creepy.

00:20:12.962 --> 00:20:15.298
Damn, so the spell had already worn off.

00:20:15.382 --> 00:20:16.841
About before...

00:20:16.925 --> 00:20:21.721
What do you intend to do if you meet Lina?

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:29.813
I'm not going to do anything
you'd have to worry about.

00:20:29.896 --> 00:20:32.941
I just want...

00:20:33.024 --> 00:20:37.404
I just want another look inside Mom's closet.

00:20:38.488 --> 00:20:43.785
<i>Mom, people say that falling
in love makes a girl beautiful,</i>

00:20:43.868 --> 00:20:48.164
<i>but does that mean she'll stay
grubby forever if she never loves anyone'?</i>

00:20:48.248 --> 00:20:51.000
<i>What about the girls of the Sisterhood?</i>

00:20:51.084 --> 00:20:53.545
<i>They</i> aren't in love with any flesh-and-blood men,

00:20:53.628 --> 00:20:56.589
<i>but they are in love with the
Three Kingdoms, trains, and dolls.</i>

00:20:56.673 --> 00:21:02.637
When his eyes met mine... could <i>I</i> have...?

00:21:04.973 --> 00:21:09.769
--I knew it! You didn't use makeup remover when you washed
your face! --Mom... Why is <i>it</i> that girls have to be pretty?

00:21:09.769 --> 00:21:11.813
<i>--We're redoing it!
--Mom... Why is it that girls have to be pretty?</i>

00:21:11.896 --> 00:21:17.861
<i>I don't want to be pretty! I really, really don't!</i>

00:21:21.281 --> 00:21:30.290
<i>I really want you to
realize that you're gorgeous</i>

00:21:30.373 --> 00:21:34.711
<i>Why haven't you realized it before this?</i>

00:21:34.794 --> 00:21:39.215
<i>It's like you've lost your heart</i>

00:21:39.299 --> 00:21:48.391
<i>I</i> want you to realize <i>it</i> right away,
right away, <i>I</i> want you to understand

00:21:48.475 --> 00:22:02.864
<i>I want you to realize it right</i> away,
<i>I want you to realize your beauty</i>

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:08.703
<i>Because you're so very beautiful</i>

00:22:08.786 --> 00:22:12.790
<i>I want to convey that to you</i>

00:22:12.874 --> 00:22:22.467
<i>Your loveliness, forever and ever</i>

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:30.892
<i>I'll be so happy if you'll
just realize your loveliness</i>

00:22:30.975 --> 00:22:35.688
<i>I</i> care about you, you know

00:22:35.772 --> 00:22:45.031
Please, realize your beauty
